  "title": "Tim B NDE 7816",
  "date": "10/10/1997",
  "content": "I was pushing on the crossbeam under the truck trying to get it off my chest. Then I was looking down on the truck. I could tell I was floating above the shop light in the garage. I could see the hood and roof of the truck. Then I was somewhere else. It was all brown. I heard a voice say, 'Your kids can't lose their dog and their dad in the same week.' A car on the highway had hit my dog four days earlier. The next thing I knew, I was looking up at the underside of the truck. The cross piece was lifted off my chest and the truck rolled further down, pinning me on my thigh. I was stuck that way for what I think was 45 minutes.",
